!.env.example

# A review agent given `isolation: worktree` gets a checkout of this repo INSIDE this repo (114).
# This machine already ignores it through `.git/info/exclude`, which is local and untracked — so
# on any other checkout a live reviewer would show up as 1,125 untracked files, one `git add -A`
# away from being committed into itself. That is the shape of the accident 062 paid for.
#
# ⚠️ **Deliberately only the worktrees, and the rest of `.claude/` is NOT ignored here.** The other
# ten Claude Code artifacts (`scheduled_tasks.json`, `agent-registry.json`, `checkpoints/`, …) are
# still covered only by `.git/info/exclude` and `~/.gitignore_global` — machine-local, exactly the
# mechanism this line exists to stop relying on. Ignoring them all in a tracked file would also
# pre-decide that no `.claude/` content may ever be committed, which is not this task's to decide.
# `**/` rather than a root anchor, matching the form `.git/info/exclude` already uses.
**/.claude/worktrees/

# Python bytecode from the mutation census/harness
__pycache__/

# The mutation harness's one repository-global tree lock (196 H2). A run in progress owns it; a
# leftover one is a machine fact for a person to look at, never something to commit.
scripts/mutations/.tree-lock/

# A table run's stream before it is published, and what an interrupted run leaves; only the
# finished mutations.txt is the table's record.
scripts/mutations/*/mutations.txt.partial*
